==Damage Distribution==
Status effect procs will occur in proportion to the amount of base damage dealt by each of the present damage types on the weapon. For example, an unmodded {{Weapon|Strun}}'s highest physical damage type is {{D|Impact}}, thus it inflicts mostly Knockback procs.

Increasing the physical or elemental damage of a weapon does not increase the duration of the associated proc (e.g. enemies won't be confused longer if {{D|Radiation}} damage is increased).

When a hit procs, the chance for an individual damage type to proc in relation to the others is:

{{MathText|Proc Type Chance {{eql}} Damage {{div}} Total Damage}}

For example, if a weapon's damage is composed of 20 {{D|Impact}}, 5 {{D|Puncture}}, 10 {{D|Slash}}, 25 {{D|Heat}}, and 50 {{D|Corrosive}}, then its total damage is {{Math|20 + 5 + 10 + 25 + 50|t=y}}. Therefore, the chance for the individual damage types to proc will be:
