==Trivia==
*Prior to {{ver|25.7}}, a status effect's duration could be increased or decreased, along with the total number of ticks in the case of damage-over-time procs, if the target's speed was altered by a Warframe power (such as {{A|Molecular Prime}} or {{A|Rest & Rage}}) according to the following formulas:
**For slowing effects: {{MathText|Effective status duration {{eql}} (base status duration) {{div}} (1 {{min}} slow % in decimals)}}
**For speeding effects: {{MathText|Effective status duration {{eql}} (base status duration) {{div}} (1 + speed up % in decimals)}}

*Prior to {{ver|27.2}}, physical procs were weighted four times more than elemental ones.
*Prior to {{ver|27.2}}, shotguns' status chance per pellet were calculated differently, instead of being the exact status chance shown in the Arsenal: {{MathText|Chance per Pellet {{eql}} 1 {{min}} (1 {{min}} Status Chance)<sup>(1 {{div}} Pellet Count)</sup>}}
**In other words, the status chance shown in the Arsenal represented the calculated probability that at least one of the weapon's pellets would proc.
**This meant that shotguns that could reach 100% status chance in the Arsenal (before [[Multishot]] mods) benefited significantly more from a status build since each pellet would proc as a result of the above equation.
**However, a shotgun that only reaches shy of 100% status chance when modded would see significantly diminished results.
***For example, a 99% '''status chance''' on a 10 pellet weapon would result in a 36.9% '''status chance per pellet'''.

